{
  "architecture": "ResNet-18 layout (BasicBlock, [2, 2, 2, 2]) at half width (32, 64, 128, 256); 3 x 3 stem at stride 2 (a CPU-scope deviation from the stride-1 stem of PRD 11.3); global average pool to a 256-d embedding, L2-normalised for retrieval",
  "g5_status": "FAIL",
  "intended_use": "A second opinion only. The encoder embeds 5 km windows at 78 m sampling of Moon, Mars and Earth terrain into 256 numbers and offers a third, always Predicted, distance family beside the deterministic terrain fingerprint. It is EXPERIMENTAL, stays outside every ranking until gate G5 passes, and never replaces the fingerprint on any card.",
  "licence": "Apache-2.0",
  "limitations": "Every encoder statistic is Predicted, a model output and not an observation. The model makes no claim about radar, trafficability, regolith mechanics or ice, and a close embedding is not evidence of an analog. It was evaluated only on 5 km windows at 78 m sampling from spatially held-out blocks; results do not transfer to other scales. The morphology probe is Unavailable because no crater labels exist in this dataset. Frozen ImageNet ResNet-18 and DINO ViT-S/8 baselines are Unavailable until their weights are fetched. Windows overlapping a target footprint are excluded by the dataset build. Training ran at a reduced CPU scope (no GPU) that departs from the PRD training recipe in data volume, epochs, batch size, precision and stem stride; each departure is listed per run in report/curves.json.",
